From 35f2df12b9868b1ec41186cca7039531f74fc45a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: overdoingism <overdoingism@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 13:52:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ggml-cuda: optional GPU keep-alive (GGML_CUDA_KEEPALIVE_MS=N
 ms, 0/unset = off)

A background thread per device launches one tiny kernel on its own stream once the device has had
no graph submission or synchronize for N ms and every submitted graph has finished (event per
submitting stream), so it never runs during prefill or decode.  For systems that power down an idle
discrete GPU and move all of its memory out (seen on Windows with the desktop on an APU).  Touches
only its own 4-byte buffer: outputs unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
